{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012J98jF7LNKSiYquEcnNt3Q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tslug: pose-review-resume-residuals\n3\tstatus: in-progress        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\n4\tcreated_at: 2026-11-27\n5\tcompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\n6\tsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\n7\tdepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\n8\tremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\n9\tpriority: 3\n10\tcomponents: pose-mcp\n11\ttask_type: bugfix\n12\tsurface: standard\n13\tdelivers: capability:review-resume-residuals\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t# Spec: pose-review-resume-residuals\n17\t\n18\t## 1. Intent\n19\t\n20\t### Goal\n21\tClose what `pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups` left open: the claim wait, a continued round whose ledger read fails, the held-path window between plan and dispatch, the recorded reason, the rounds documentation and the remaining test gaps.\n22\t\n23\t### Business value\n24\tThe spec closed on 2026-11-27 with follow-ups in its Final Report (round 1, N4–N5) and its approving attestation (round 2, N6–N11).\n25\t\n26\t### Constraints\n27\tEach item keeps the behaviour its origin spec delivered; a fix that changes an answer states it as a decision.\n28\t\n29\t### Non-goals\n30\tReopening the decisions of the origin spec.\n31\t\n32\t## 2. Requirements\n33\t\n34\t### Functional\n35\t- R1: The wait for another resume's claim shall report a completed continuation as such (and to a handoff as already continued), honour cancellation, read the ledger cheaply, and turn a claim conflict after the winner finished into the recorded result (round 1 N4, round 2 N9).\n36\t- R2: A continued round whose previous runtime name cannot be read from the ledger shall record that in the run instead of moving its checkout silently (round 1 N5, round 2 N10).\n37\t- R3: A thread path taken between the plan and the dispatch shall not fail the run after its attempt is reserved, nor ask to remove a directory another run may hold (round 2, N6).\n38\t- R4: The recorded reason shall name the held path, and an lstat error other than not-exist shall not count as a free path (round 2, N7).\n39\t- R5: The review rounds documentation, in both locales and the embedded copies, shall list the held-path condition for opening a new session (round 2, N11).\n40\t- R6: Tests shall reach the exclusive take after a replan, resume end to end a run whose recorded random name differs from the stable one, and cover the claim-failure removal and the handoff plan's pending branch (rounds 1 N3, 2 N8).\n41\t\n42\t### Non-functional\n43\tExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n44\t\n45\t### Security\n46\tNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n47\t\n48\t### Compatibility\n49\tRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n50\t\n51\t## 3. Technical Plan\n52\t\n53\t### Affected areas\n54\t`pose-mcp`: `review_dispatch.go`, `review_rounds.go`, `delegation_handoff.go`, the manual in both locales, and their tests.\n55\t\n56\t### Artifacts\n57\t- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\n58\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n59\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n60\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n61\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\n62\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\n63\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_rounds_test.go\n64\t- modified: POSE.md\n65\t- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n66\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n67\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n68\t\n69\t### Delivery targets\n70\t- capability:review-resume-residuals module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n71\t\n72\t### Accepted limits\n73\t- L1: Three guards have no failing test: the claim-publication conflict that returns the winner's record, an lstat error other than not-exist counting as held, and a continued round whose ledger read fails. Accepted because each needs a race, a permission fault or a ledger fault the fixtures cannot make deterministically, and each fails toward refusing or recording, never toward sharing a directory.\n74\t\n75\t### API/contract changes\n76\tA continued round whose checkout could not follow its session records it among the run's `safety.limitations`. A resume or handoff that meets another's recorded continuation returns that record.\n77\t\n78\t### Data/storage changes\n79\tNone.\n80\t\n81\t### Technical risks\n82\tA resume waits up to two seconds for another resume's claim, now only while a claim file exists.\n83\t\n84\t## 4. Tasks\n85\t\n86\t### Planning\n87\t- [x] Confirm each requirement against the current engine before starting.\n88\t\n89\t### Implementation\n90\t- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n91\t\n92\t### Validation\n93\t- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n94\t\n95\t## 5. Decisions\n96\t\n97\t## 6. Validation\n98\t\n99\t### Strategy\n100\tEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n101\t\n102\t### Deterministic checks\n103\t\n104\t#### Test\n105\t- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n106\t\n107\t### Execution log\n108\t- 2026-11-27: R1 `awaitContinuationClaim` returns a recorded continuation as the result, reads the ledger only once a claim file exists and stops with its context; a claim conflict replans to the recorded or pending continuation. R2/R3 `runtimeSourceFor` says why a continued round cannot take the previous name, and a path taken after the plan falls back to the round's own directory; both are recorded in `safety.limitations`. R4 the reason names the held path, and an lstat error other than not-exist counts as held. R5 the rounds paragraph in both locales and the embedded copies. `TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed` and `TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread` fail with the cancellation, the named path or the fallback mutated out; L1 lists what has no test.\n109\t\n110\t### Results summary\n111\tThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n112\t\n113\t### Requirement trace\n114\t- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestRunContinuityConcurrentResumeLaunchesOnce\n115\t- R2 [satisfied] (accepted limit L1)\n116\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n117\t- R4 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n118\t- R5 [satisfied] (manual, both locales)\n119\t- R6 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n120\t\n121\t### Known gaps\n122\tThe random-name end-to-end resume and the handoff plan's pending branch remain untested (R6 in part); see Follow-ups.\n123\t\n124\t## 7. Final Report\n125\t\n126\t### Delivered scope\n127\tThe claim wait returns recorded continuations and stops with its context; a continued round that cannot keep its checkout path works in its own directory and says so; held paths are named; the manual lists the condition.\n128\t\n129\t### Files and modules changed\n130\t`pose-mcp` review dispatch, rounds, resume and handoff plans; the manual in both locales and its embedded copies.\n131\t\n132\t### Validation executed\n133\t`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n134\t\n135\t### Residual risks\n136\tL1 above.\n137\t\n138\t### Follow-ups\n139\tOrigin: `pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups` (done 2026-11-27).\n140\t- [open] Resume end to end a run whose recorded runtime name is a random one of an earlier engine, and reach the handoff plan's pending branch in a test (R6 in part). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-27)\n141\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"69ecc81d-1cd0-4874-8604-c633490b17cd","timestamp":"2026-11-27T23:07:43.452Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-668ca2f6e0/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md","content":"---\nslug: pose-review-resume-residuals\nstatus: in-progress        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\ncreated_at: 2026-11-27\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority: 3\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface: standard\ndelivers: capability:review-resume-residuals\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-review-resume-residuals\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nClose what `pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups` left open: the claim wait, a continued round whose ledger read fails, the held-path window between plan and dispatch, the recorded reason, the rounds documentation and the remaining test gaps.\n\n### Business value\nThe spec closed on 2026-11-27 with follow-ups in its Final Report (round 1, N4–N5) and its approving attestation (round 2, N6–N11).\n\n### Constraints\nEach item keeps the behaviour its origin spec delivered; a fix that changes an answer states it as a decision.\n\n### Non-goals\nReopening the decisions of the origin spec.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: The wait for another resume's claim shall report a completed continuation as such (and to a handoff as already continued), honour cancellation, read the ledger cheaply, and turn a claim conflict after the winner finished into the recorded result (round 1 N4, round 2 N9).\n- R2: A continued round whose previous runtime name cannot be read from the ledger shall record that in the run instead of moving its checkout silently (round 1 N5, round 2 N10).\n- R3: A thread path taken between the plan and the dispatch shall not fail the run after its attempt is reserved, nor ask to remove a directory another run may hold (round 2, N6).\n- R4: The recorded reason shall name the held path, and an lstat error other than not-exist shall not count as a free path (round 2, N7).\n- R5: The review rounds documentation, in both locales and the embedded copies, shall list the held-path condition for opening a new session (round 2, N11).\n- R6: Tests shall reach the exclusive take after a replan, resume end to end a run whose recorded random name differs from the stable one, and cover the claim-failure removal and the handoff plan's pending branch (rounds 1 N3, 2 N8).\n\n### Non-functional\nExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n\n### Security\nNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n\n### Compatibility\nRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n`pose-mcp`: `review_dispatch.go`, `review_rounds.go`, `delegation_handoff.go`, the manual in both locales, and their tests.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_rounds_test.go\n- modified: POSE.md\n- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n\n### Delivery targets\n- capability:review-resume-residuals module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n\n### Accepted limits\n- L1: Three guards have no failing test: the claim-publication conflict that returns the winner's record, an lstat error other than not-exist counting as held, and a continued round whose ledger read fails. Accepted because each needs a race, a permission fault or a ledger fault the fixtures cannot make deterministically, and each fails toward refusing or recording, never toward sharing a directory.\n\n### API/contract changes\nA continued round whose checkout could not follow its session records it among the run's `safety.limitations`. A resume or handoff that meets another's recorded continuation returns that record.\n\n### Data/storage changes\nNone.\n\n### Technical risks\nA resume waits up to two seconds for another resume's claim, now only while a claim file exists.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Planning\n- [x] Confirm each requirement against the current engine before starting.\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n\n### Validation\n- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Execution log\n- 2026-11-27: R1 `awaitContinuationClaim` returns a recorded continuation as the result, reads the ledger only once a claim file exists and stops with its context; a claim conflict replans to the recorded or pending continuation. R2/R3 `runtimeSourceFor` says why a continued round cannot take the previous name, and a path taken after the plan falls back to the round's own directory; both are recorded in `safety.limitations`. R4 the reason names the held path, and an lstat error other than not-exist counts as held. R5 the rounds paragraph in both locales and the embedded copies. `TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed` and `TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread` fail with the cancellation, the named path or the fallback mutated out; L1 lists what has no test.\n\n### Results summary\nThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestRunContinuityConcurrentResumeLaunchesOnce\n- R2 [satisfied] (accepted limit L1)\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n- R4 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n- R5 [satisfied] (manual, both locales)\n- R6 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n\n### Known gaps\nThe random-name end-to-end resume and the handoff plan's pending branch remain untested (R6 in part); see Follow-ups.\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nThe claim wait returns recorded continuations and stops with its context; a continued round that cannot keep its checkout path works in its own directory and says so; held paths are named; the manual lists the condition.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n`pose-mcp` review dispatch, rounds, resume and handoff plans; the manual in both locales and its embedded copies.\n\n### Validation executed\n`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n\n### Residual risks\nL1 above.\n\n### Follow-ups\nOrigin: `pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups` (done 2026-11-27).\n- [open] Resume end to end a run whose recorded runtime name is a random one of an earlier engine, and reach the handoff plan's pending branch in a test (R6 in part). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-27)\n","numLines":141,"startLine":1,"totalLines":141}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012J98jF7LNKSiYquEcnNt3Q","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
