{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChUJBkhUiYVPFRqSWcSiD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_read_input_tokens":133637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":686},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"51bf4e00-85ec-4c40-9467-cf45e7c3748b","timestamp":"2026-11-27T23:26:07.202Z","request_id":"req_011ChUJBk9EpmyRDEjZoD4iu","thinking_duration_ms":21482,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChUJBkhUiYVPFRqSWcSiD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YPzGG2AqyD7J7cBTsTW5gk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat <<'EOF' | \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":2263,\"summary\":\"awaitContinuationClaim returns any recorded continuation without checking its kind or agent. A resume that loses the race to a completed handoff gets that handoff run as its own successful result (review_dispatch.go:761-763; PlanReviewResume at review_run_continuity.go:440-444, returned by the replan at review_dispatch.go:740-741), bypassing the 'handed off; it is not resumed' refusal at review_run_continuity.go:423-424. A handoff that loses inside takeContinuationRuntimeDir to a resume or to another agent's handoff also returns that run as success instead of 'already continued' (delegation_handoff.go:339-342), contrary to R1. Established by code reading.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\".pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\",\"line\":119,\"summary\":\"R6 is traced satisfied but is not delivered: no test makes the exclusive take refuse after a successful replan (review_dispatch.go:764-766 uncovered; the dispatch-beside-a-directory test is refused earlier by the replan), none covers the claim-failure removal (769-771 uncovered), and Known gaps admits the random-name resume and the handoff pending branch are missing. R1's recorded-continuation returns (review_dispatch.go:761-763 and the existing return of awaitContinuationClaim, review_run_continuity.go:440-445, delegation_handoff.go:357-361) are also uncovered by the focused tests and are outside L1, which names only the claim-publication conflict.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":2270,\"summary\":\"A cancelled wait returns (nil,nil), so takeContinuationRuntimeDir returns the 'runtime directory already exists ... remove it' error instead of the context error, advising removal of a directory another resume may hold. The waits reached through replanContinuation use context.Background() (review_run_continuity.go:435, delegation_handoff.go:352), so cancellation is not honoured there for up to about two seconds.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":774,\"summary\":\"After a claim conflict, a replan that refuses because the winner was a different continuation (resume lost to a handoff, or handoff lost to another agent) is discarded and the raw publication conflict is returned instead of the 'already continued' or 'handed off' answer.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"POSE.md\",\"line\":956,\"summary\":\"The manual (both locales) says a held previous checkout path opens a new session, but a path taken after the plan keeps the continued session and moves its checkout (review_dispatch.go:848-858); the resumed session may still refer to the old path, which can hold another live run's checkout. The manual does not describe this, and spec section 5 records no decision for this or for returning recorded continuations, although its Constraints require one when a fix changes an answer.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N6\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\",\"line\":701,\"summary\":\"previousRoundCheckoutHeld is evaluated twice; if the holder removes the directory between line 695 and line 701 the recorded reason is 'checkout path  is still in use' with no path. A path that only failed lstat is also reported as still in use.\"}\n],\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Checked L1 and the spec's risk statement against the code. Verified: directories are created with exclusive Mkdir (review_dispatch.go:2166), the fallback takes the new attempt's own name exclusively, and an lstat error counts as held. L1's three guards remain untested, accepted by the spec; the untested recorded-continuation returns fall outside it (N2). That a resumed session tolerates a moved checkout is an unverified assumption (N5).\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N3\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Read the CLI consumers of resume and handoff plans (delegate.go, delegate_handoff.go); signatures changed only inside package pose. The mismatched-continuation behaviour is reported as N1.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"A moved checkout is recorded in safety.limitations with its reason and the thread reason names the held path; the minor empty-path race is N6.\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-1b92e8ee6f296c99\",\"rationale\":\"The design assessment observed no structural deltas, so there is nothing to map. Exclusive directory creation as the lock, claim-file gating of ledger reads, and a fallback to the attempt's own directory address the causes behind R1 to R4; the gap in the R1 result selection is N1.\"},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N5\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N3\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Compared the ten files of change set cs-61d69e9d2ff2 with the spec's artifacts and R1 to R6; no unrelated behaviour was found in them. Other commits in the range belong to other specs. Incomplete delivery is N2.\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined path derivation and directory creation: the recorded runtime name is bounded by a regular expression, creation is exclusive, nothing removes a directory the dispatch did not create, and session reading is unchanged. The new records include a local temporary path, which R4 asks for. The old-path reference of a resumed session is reported in N5.\"},\n{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"The change is small and local with no new abstraction beyond an error type carrying the recorded run. A smaller alternative for the late-held path (open a new session) would need replanning after attempt reservation; the chosen fallback is proportionate while the run records the move. It would be invalidated if resumed agents depended on the old absolute path.\"}\n],\n\"tools\":[\n{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-resume-residuals --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0, with repository-wide orphan warnings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-1b92e8ee6f296c99\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no structural deltas.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Ran with --no-persist; the gaps seen in the output tail concern HTTP consumers outside this change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; the scan reports itself incomplete because two older specs could not be read.\"},\n{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; it cannot pass before an approving attestation and the spec is not done.\"},\n{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; it cannot pass before the attestation of this review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0 with zero findings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Not rerun: the sealed result covers it. Focused tests run here fail in internal/cli where the sandbox's /home ownership blocks task state; internal/pose passes.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Not rerun: the sealed result covers it; the sandbox limitation is the same.\"}\n]}\n```\nEOF","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_read_input_tokens":133637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":686},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"c6a874b2-59fe-44db-911f-7160d503ce05","timestamp":"2026-11-27T23:26:27.009Z","request_id":"req_011ChUJBk9EpmyRDEjZoD4iu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YPzGG2AqyD7J7cBTsTW5gk":{"command":"cat <<'EOF' | \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":2263,\"summary\":\"awaitContinuationClaim returns any recorded continuation without checking its kind or agent. A resume that loses the race to a completed handoff gets that handoff run as its own successful result (review_dispatch.go:761-763; PlanReviewResume at review_run_continuity.go:440-444, returned by the replan at review_dispatch.go:740-741), bypassing the 'handed off; it is not resumed' refusal at review_run_continuity.go:423-424. A handoff that loses inside takeContinuationRuntimeDir to a resume or to another agent's handoff also returns that run as success instead of 'already continued' (delegation_handoff.go:339-342), contrary to R1. Established by code reading.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\".pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\",\"line\":119,\"summary\":\"R6 is traced satisfied but is not delivered: no test makes the exclusive take refuse after a successful replan (review_dispatch.go:764-766 uncovered; the dispatch-beside-a-directory test is refused earlier by the replan), none covers the claim-failure removal (769-771 uncovered), and Known gaps admits the random-name resume and the handoff pending branch are missing. R1's recorded-continuation returns (review_dispatch.go:761-763 and the existing return of awaitContinuationClaim, review_run_continuity.go:440-445, delegation_handoff.go:357-361) are also uncovered by the focused tests and are outside L1, which names only the claim-publication conflict.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":2270,\"summary\":\"A cancelled wait returns (nil,nil), so takeContinuationRuntimeDir returns the 'runtime directory already exists ... remove it' error instead of the context error, advising removal of a directory another resume may hold. The waits reached through replanContinuation use context.Background() (review_run_continuity.go:435, delegation_handoff.go:352), so cancellation is not honoured there for up to about two seconds.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":774,\"summary\":\"After a claim conflict, a replan that refuses because the winner was a different continuation (resume lost to a handoff, or handoff lost to another agent) is discarded and the raw publication conflict is returned instead of the 'already continued' or 'handed off' answer.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"POSE.md\",\"line\":956,\"summary\":\"The manual (both locales) says a held previous checkout path opens a new session, but a path taken after the plan keeps the continued session and moves its checkout (review_dispatch.go:848-858); the resumed session may still refer to the old path, which can hold another live run's checkout. The manual does not describe this, and spec section 5 records no decision for this or for returning recorded continuations, although its Constraints require one when a fix changes an answer.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N6\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\",\"line\":701,\"summary\":\"previousRoundCheckoutHeld is evaluated twice; if the holder removes the directory between line 695 and line 701 the recorded reason is 'checkout path  is still in use' with no path. A path that only failed lstat is also reported as still in use.\"}\n],\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Checked L1 and the spec's risk statement against the code. Verified: directories are created with exclusive Mkdir (review_dispatch.go:2166), the fallback takes the new attempt's own name exclusively, and an lstat error counts as held. L1's three guards remain untested, accepted by the spec; the untested recorded-continuation returns fall outside it (N2). That a resumed session tolerates a moved checkout is an unverified assumption (N5).\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N3\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Read the CLI consumers of resume and handoff plans (delegate.go, delegate_handoff.go); signatures changed only inside package pose. The mismatched-continuation behaviour is reported as N1.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"A moved checkout is recorded in safety.limitations with its reason and the thread reason names the held path; the minor empty-path race is N6.\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-1b92e8ee6f296c99\",\"rationale\":\"The design assessment observed no structural deltas, so there is nothing to map. Exclusive directory creation as the lock, claim-file gating of ledger reads, and a fallback to the attempt's own directory address the causes behind R1 to R4; the gap in the R1 result selection is N1.\"},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N5\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N3\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Compared the ten files of change set cs-61d69e9d2ff2 with the spec's artifacts and R1 to R6; no unrelated behaviour was found in them. Other commits in the range belong to other specs. Incomplete delivery is N2.\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined path derivation and directory creation: the recorded runtime name is bounded by a regular expression, creation is exclusive, nothing removes a directory the dispatch did not create, and session reading is unchanged. The new records include a local temporary path, which R4 asks for. The old-path reference of a resumed session is reported in N5.\"},\n{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"The change is small and local with no new abstraction beyond an error type carrying the recorded run. A smaller alternative for the late-held path (open a new session) would need replanning after attempt reservation; the chosen fallback is proportionate while the run records the move. It would be invalidated if resumed agents depended on the old absolute path.\"}\n],\n\"tools\":[\n{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-resume-residuals --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0, with repository-wide orphan warnings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-1b92e8ee6f296c99\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no structural deltas.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Ran with --no-persist; the gaps seen in the output tail concern HTTP consumers outside this change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; the scan reports itself incomplete because two older specs could not be read.\"},\n{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; it cannot pass before an approving attestation and the spec is not done.\"},\n{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; it cannot pass before the attestation of this review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0 with zero findings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Not rerun: the sealed result covers it. Focused tests run here fail in internal/cli where the sandbox's /home ownership blocks task state; internal/pose passes.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Not rerun: the sealed result covers it; the sandbox limitation is the same.\"}\n]}\n```\nEOF","timeout":300000}}}
